# `npm version` in a workspace defaults to also re-running a workspace-wide
# install to refresh the lockfile, and that install runs the `prepare`
# lifecycle script of EVERY workspace in the repo.
#
# That default breaks npm releases here. @semantic-release/npm's `prepare`
# step is only `npm version <version>` in the published package's pkgRoot
# (node_modules/@semantic-release/npm/lib/prepare.js), so each of the three
# packages .releaserc.yaml publishes triggers one such install. Three
# vendored reference-implementation workspaces declare a `prepare` script —
# @pdpp/cli, @pdpp/mcp-server, and @pdpp/read-core, all `npm run build` —
# and none of them is published by that workflow. Their builds are pure
# collateral, so a failure in any one of them aborts a release whose own
# artifacts are fine. Run 34369074799 failed exactly that way: OIDC
# succeeded, connector-protocol's prepare completed, then
# collector-runtime's `npm version` triggered the install, @pdpp/cli's build
# ran, and its `tsc` failed — nothing published.
#
# Disabling the update makes `npm version` write the version field and stop,
# which is all that prepare step needs. The published packages are still
# built: each declares its own `prepack`, which `npm publish` runs for the
# package being published.
#
# This lives in the repo .npmrc rather than the release workflow's env
# because it is a property of this workspace, not of one CI step: any
# `npm version` run here (a local release rehearsal, a future workflow) hits
# the same collateral builds. A project .npmrc is also the channel that
# actually survives semantic-release, which passes `--userconfig <its own
# npmrc>` to every npm call — that flag replaces the *user* config file and
# leaves the project file in effect.
#
# Trade-off: `npm version` no longer refreshes package-lock.json's version
# field for the bumped workspace. That is not load-bearing here — the three
# published packages carry placeholder versions that @semantic-release/npm
# overwrites at publish time, and the lockfile is not part of any published
# tarball.
workspaces-update=false
